Z||000011||HummelHund||08-31-2001||09:09 PM||||If one was to gut the car interior-wise and maybe even take off a few body panels, wouldn't replacing the wiring harness be fairly easy, just tedious? I've got an 84' with a duke that's going to need a rebuild eventually, but if I could just grab a 2.8 V6 with cradle, a fuel pump, and a wiring harness, wouldn't it be a pretty straightforward job of swapping engines?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>84' SE 2M4 WS6 (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
